      "start": 10.49,
      "end": 17.24,
      "text": "Fireworks really need the camera to stay still for a second or two. Do you have a tripod, or anything to rest the camera on?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 21.39,
      "end": 30.03,
      "text": "Great. Set focus manually to infinity, use a low ISO, and an exposure of about two to four seconds. That turns sparks into long trails."
